From 64dc230a846924d6e666d79112b62e1ff746ed68 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Meir Dick <mdick85@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 15:17:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: tas2783: keep the whole port for a firmware-described
 amp

173cb3147ba2 ("ASoC: tas2783-sdw: split a stereo stream across the two
mono amps") narrows each amp to one channel of the stereo stream, keyed
off its component prefix. That assumes the amp plays whatever single
channel it receives, which holds when the driver initialises it from
tas2783_init_seq: the sequence sets the same DSP posture on every part,
and every part then reads the first channel it is given.

When platform firmware describes the SmartAmp function, the driver
initialises the part from that description instead, and the posture its
firmware image programmed survives. On the HP EliteBook X G2i with BIOS
01.02.02, the two right-hand parts keep posture 4, which reads the
second channel of the port. Narrowed to one channel, they read an empty
slot and the right side is silent. Fed the whole stereo port, each part
picks its own side.

Skip the narrowing when sa_func_data is set. Parts without SDCA function
data keep the split.

Signed-off-by: Meir Dick <mdick85@gmail.com>
---
 sound/soc/codecs/tas2783-sdw.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/tas2783-sdw.c b/sound/soc/codecs/tas2783-sdw.c
index 8c5983c18..dc5ab0800 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/tas2783-sdw.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/tas2783-sdw.c
@@ -1095,9 +1095,18 @@ static s32 tas_sdw_hw_params(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream,
 	 * the popcount of ch_mask and never looks at which bit it is - but
 	 * from the amp's position in the codec order of the DAI link, which
 	 * on these boards matches the prefix numbering.
+	 *
+	 * Not when platform firmware describes the SmartAmp function. The
+	 * part is then initialised from that description instead of
+	 * tas2783_init_seq, and keeps the DSP posture its firmware image
+	 * programmed for its side: the right-hand parts read the second
+	 * channel of the port. Narrowed to one channel they read an empty
+	 * slot and play nothing. Fed the whole port, each part picks its
+	 * own channel.
 	 */
 	if (substream->stream == SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_PLAYBACK &&
-	    params_channels(params) == 2 && component->name_prefix) {
+	    params_channels(params) == 2 && component->name_prefix &&
+	    !tas_dev->sa_func_data) {
 		const char *idx_str = strrchr(component->name_prefix, '-');
 		unsigned long idx;
 
